  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (STANDARD). Read DS-5 §C5.7 + Program.cs:483-486's existing deferral comment.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Bicep KV-ref">Add the EnvVarValues__ClientSecret app setting as a KV reference to the appropriate secret name, on the .Worker site.</step>
    <step order="2" name="NFR-05 validation">Extend H7's existing IOptions validation to fail-fast if this key is absent, matching the established Tier-1 config pattern.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Tests">Add a fail-fast test (absent key -&gt; startup/validation failure, not silent empty-string proceed).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Build + verify">dotnet build 0 errors; dotnet test green (existing H7 tests unmodified + the new fail-fast test).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>Auth-v4 coordination (spec.md FR-39): if the customer BFF's Dataverse credential path is FULLY Managed-Identity-based (no client-secret concept remaining anywhere in the customer stamp) by the time this task executes -- i.e., `spaarke-auth-v4-dataverse-MI`'s migration has completed for the Dataverse path specifically -- STOP and escalate to the project owner: this task RETIRES (there is no `EnvVarValues:ClientSecret` to wire at all), rather than being executed against a credential shape that no longer exists.</trigger>
